visrtx provides CMake integration via ANARI. After loading the ANARI SDK you
can use VisRTX devices at runtime without any additional CMake wiring:

    find_package(anari REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE anari::anari)

The VisRTX shared libraries are ANARI back-end plug-ins that are discovered
automatically when they are on the library search path.

-- Feature notes --

  gl   (default)  OpenGL rendering device — no extra requirements.
  rtx             OptiX/CUDA RTX device. Requires:
                    - NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit 12+ (system install)
                    - NVIDIA OptiX SDK 7.7 / 8.x / 9.0 (system install)
                  If OptiX is not in a standard location, set:
                    OPTIX_INSTALL_DIR=<path>  (env variable, read by the port)
                  or pass -DOptiX_INSTALL_DIR=<path> to your CMake configure.
